 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that times out is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all, with a growing pause before each retry: 2, 4, 6
+and then 8 seconds, so a member can wait up to 20 seconds longer on the confirmation page. `ATTEMPTS` and
+`BACKOFF_SECONDS` in `larder/capture.py` set them.
+
+Captures used to make 3 attempts back to back, within one second. Every Friday from 17:00 to 19:00, the gateway's
+peak, its status page shows slow responses, so all three attempts landed in the same slow minute: one Friday 58 pantry
+orders were confirmed but never charged, and a payments volunteer captured them by hand from the gateway's dashboard
+the next morning. Switching gateways was ruled out while its contract runs. Replayed against the gateway's sandbox,
+5 attempts spaced 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds apart would have charged 57 of those 58; the longer wait on the confirmation
+page was judged better than a volunteer capturing orders by hand.
 
 Every attempt to capture one pantry order sends the same idempotency key, the one its first attempt used. The gateway
 can report a timeout after it has already charged the card, and it charges again for a new key: in 2024 retries that
 drew a fresh key for each attempt charged 41 members twice.
 
+## Known limits
+
+- A capture can still time out on all 5 attempts during the gateway's Friday peak: in the replay, 1 pantry order in 58
+  did. It stays confirmed but uncharged; follow [the gateway-timeouts runbook](../runbooks/gateway-timeouts.md) to find
+  it.
